<title>COLOMBIA: Foreign portfolio investment edges up in Colombia.</title>
<headline>Foreign portfolio investment edges up in Colombia.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portfolio investment by foreign funds operating in Colombia edged up a paper-thin 0.3 percent to 1.02 trillion pesos ($980 million) in August, the Securities Superintendency said.</p>
<p>It said the increase was 1.7 percent when measured in dollar terms, however, and that the peso total represented a 23.9 percent increase over August 1995.</p>
<p>-- Javier Mozzo, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944</p>
